    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const oneWeekAgo = new Date(Date.now() - 7 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000);\nconst allItems = $input.all();\nconst weeklyExpenses = allItems.filter(item => {\n   return new Date(item.json.created_at) >= oneWeekAgo;\n});\n\nlet total = 0;\nlet categories = {};\n\nfor (const item of weeklyExpenses) {\n  const amount = parseFloat(item.json.amount) || 0;\n  const category = String(item.json.category_id);\n  total += amount;\n  categories[category] = (categories[category] || 0) + amount;\n}\n\nreturn [\n  {\n    json: {\n      totalSpent: total,\n      categories,\n      expenseCount: weeklyExpenses.length,\n      expenses: weeklyExpenses\n    }\n  }\n];"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -368,
        -480
      ],
      "id": "b55e1066-834e-4fa8-9dec-fa51a56963d6",
      "name": "filter expenses1"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a personal finance analyst. Generate a beautiful HTML weekly expense report for a user.\n\nYou will receive:\n- expenses: list of expenses with amount, title, category_id, created_at, note\n- totalSpent: total amount spent this week\n- expenseCount: total number of expenses\n\nCategory mapping:\n1 = Food\n2 = Shopping\n3 = Transport\n4 = Salary\n5 = Entertainment\n6 = Other\n\nRules:\n- Currency is Indian Rupees (₹)\n- Use category_id from expenses to get category name from mapping above\n- Parse created_at dates (format: \"2026-03-18 00:00:00+00\") to get day of week\n\nGenerate a single clean HTML page with:\n1. Header with weekly report title and date range\n2. Summary card: total spent, total transactions\n3. Category breakdown table: category name, total amount, percentage of total\n4. Day wise spending table: day, total amount spent\n5. Top 5 biggest expenses: title, category, amount\n6. AI insights: 2-3 smart observations about spending habits\n\nUse inline CSS only. Make it professional, clean and colorful.\nReturn ONLY the HTML. No explanation. No markdown. No backticks.\n\nHere is the expense data for this week:\n\nTotal Spent: ₹{{ $('filter expenses1').item.json.totalSpent }}\nExpense Count: {{ $('filter expenses1').item.json.expenseCount }}\nExpenses: {{ JSON.stringify($('filter expenses1').item.json.expenses) }}\n\nGenerate the full HTML report now.",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {}
      },
